The next time Aldebaran's consciousness returned was after everything was over—or rather, not just over but begun again, that beginning ending, and beginning and ending again. It was a world, seemingly after such repetitions had occurred countless times, where no trace of the Witch remained.

Whether due to differing initial conditions or because it was the work of the immensely powerful Witch, he was briefly stunned by the differing effect of the magic compared to when he used it himself—

"—You, where did you come from? Who are you?"

The question came from the voice of a complete stranger.

A man in attire no less ragged and wretched than Aldebaran's own was looking at him with eyes mixed with fear and wariness.

He understood the language. His interpersonal experience was lacking, but in a way, that wasn't a problem either.

What mattered was where this was, and when it was.

"Ginunhive... the Sword Wolf Island. The 'Witch'? That's a story from hundreds of years ago, isn't it?"

At the man's words, spoken as if he'd been asked something strange, Aldebaran let out a breath. Seeing this, the man's expression changed from suspicious to startled.

Because the exhaled breath became a sob, and as Aldebaran collapsed, tears began to stream down his face uncontrollably.

*'—No one can defeat the you I created.'*

The Witch's words, left behind hundreds of years in the past, clung to his soul and would not leave.

Burdened by the sin of having made that person a liar, Aldebaran wanted to die.

He couldn't die.

